signal.description:
Emitted by the [code]event[/code] statement in TamaScript. [param name] is the event name; [param args] holds the evaluated arguments (quoted strings pass through as [String], numeric expressions as [float]). Fire-and-forget: the script does not block. Connect a single handler and dispatch on [param name] to react to script-driven events such as sound effects or score changes.
[codeblock]
func _ready():
    TamaManager.event_fired.connect(_on_event_fired)

func _on_event_fired(name: String, args: Array) -> void:
    if name == "sfx":
        play_sfx(args[0])
[/codeblock]
